# {{ project_name }} — Project Instructions

Extends praxis-kit's rules in `~/.claude/rules/` (global). Where the two conflict, this file wins. Neither file overrides
`CONSTITUTION.md`.

## Tenancy mode

**`{{ tenancy_mode }}`**, declared at bootstrap. praxis-kit's `rules/glossary.md` defines the modes:

{% if tenancy_mode == "multi-tenant" -%}
- When to pick: B2B SaaS, multiple customer orgs share one deployment
- Implications: `tenant_id` / `org_id` scoping NON-NEGOTIABLE on every data-touching endpoint and table. BOLA checks, cross-tenant returns 404 not 403. Apply `isolating-multi-tenant-llm` skill
{%- elif tenancy_mode == "single-tenant" -%}
- When to pick: Internal tool, one-customer build, multi-user app for one org
- Implications: User-level ownership checks NON-NEGOTIABLE. NO `tenant_id` column — BOLA becomes ownership-check (object.owner_id == user.id). Auth + RBAC still required
{%- else -%}
- When to pick: Personal tool, research code, single-user CLI, library
- Implications: No scoping rules; auth itself OPTIONAL. Input validation, SSRF, security headers, secrets lifecycle, supply-chain rules still apply
{%- endif %}


## Stage

**`{{ stage }}`**, declared at bootstrap. `CONSTITUTION.md` §4, next to the global `CLAUDE.md`, defines the stages and lists the practices each one switches on:

{% if stage == "explore" -%}
- True of the project: no real users and no real data
- It leaves the stage when: the first real user or real record arrives, or the code is thrown away
{%- elif stage == "build" -%}
- True of the project: real users or real data, but nobody has been promised availability
- It leaves the stage when: availability is promised, by a contract, a service level or a launch
{%- elif stage == "run" -%}
- True of the project: availability is promised, and the code changes actively
- It leaves the stage when: change is mostly fixes and upgrades
{%- else -%}
- True of the project: availability is promised, and change is mostly fixes and upgrades
- It leaves the stage when: it is retired or rebuilt
{%- endif %}


Changing stage is a decision with an owner: record it here and in an ADR.

